      "content": "In the 5.5 to 7.0 pH range, iron and manganese are generally more readily available to grapevines compared to highly alkaline soils. Within this slightly acidic to neutral window, essential micronutrients are less likely to precipitate out of the soil solution. However, even in this range, very high clay content or specific mineral compositions can still inhibit uptake. Monitoring nutrient levels is crucial to ensure the vines receive adequate nourishment for optimal grape quality.",
