      "content": "Several other soil factors can impede nutrient availability even with optimal $\\text{pH}$. High levels of organic matter, while generally beneficial, can sometimes sequester micronutrients through complexation, reducing their immediate plant uptake. Furthermore, the presence of certain soil microbes can alter nutrient cycling rates, either reducing or enhancing availability depending on the specific consortium. Lastly, root physiology issues or *rhizosphere* dynamics—the immediate area around the roots—can create localized conditions that starve the vine of essential, soluble ions.",
